## Notes for the reviewer

- The plan's prose says `SCRAMBLE_GLYPHS` has sixteen characters; the literal it gives (`!<>-_\/[]{}=+*^?#`) has seventeen. The test asserts the literal string, not a count.
- AC-18 axe: the runtime is frozen by the hidden-tab pause (AC-16) and Playwright's clock is then resumed so axe's timers run. If axe reports a color-contrast result on a partially clipped or opacity-0 element, that is an implementation or PRD question, not a test to loosen.
- Mid-step moments carry at least about 50 ms of margin because `data-build-progress` has a 1 percent resolution and the loops advance the clock 20 ms per slice.

## Revision 1 (after test-reviewer R-GREEN-LEGITIMATE CHANGES_REQUESTED)

No AC outcome and no lifecycle ledger entry changed; the ledger above is preserved as written. Three red results, each classified:

1. Bad test, fixed. tests/unit/effect-timing.test.ts "opens the clip from a 10 percent inset...": `expect(popInset(1)).toBe(0)` received 8.88e-16, a floating-point residue of `-4 * (1 - (p - 0.7) / 0.3)`. Now `toBeCloseTo(0, 9)`. The AC property (the clip settles at 0) is unchanged and still discriminative.
2. Bad test, fixed. tests/e2e/effects-hero.spec.ts "resolves the intro line by line ... then pops the buttons": it read `clip-path` from the `data-build-target="links"` wrapper. The plan (Task 5, pop) says the pop clips "the children of the target (its direct element children ...)" and the wrapper itself is only made live; src/runtime/effects.ts `pop` does exactly that, so the wrapper's inline clip is empty by design. The probe in tests/e2e/support/effects.ts now also reads `childClips` (inline clip-path of each direct child) and the test asserts at least one child and that every child clip matches `^inset`. The other assertions (wrapper `data-build-fx` null, pointer-events not none) are untouched.
3. Implementation defect, test kept unchanged. tests/e2e/effects-layout.spec.ts "never adds horizontal scroll while the hero elements are created at 375px" measured a 2 px overflow at hero t=1600 (limit 0). The PRD (AC-4) and Stage 2 require that the page never scrolls horizontally. Suspected cause: src/styles/build-layer.css `.sp-build-fx` (and `.sp-build-layer`) is `position: absolute; width: 100%; height: 0` with no horizontal overflow clipping, and `.sp-select-handle` corner squares (6 px, offset -3 px) plus the selection box placed from `docRect` can extend past the viewport edge on a narrow screen. Evidence status: the test-writer has no shell in this session, so the exact overflowing element was not measured; the diagnosis is from the CSS and the orchestrator's read, and must be confirmed by the Implementer (for example by logging the element whose right edge exceeds the viewport at t=1600). The limit stays at 0; the test must not be loosened. The suite is therefore expected to stay red on this one case until the implementation is fixed.

## Revision 2 (after second test-reviewer R-GREEN-LEGITIMATE CHANGES_REQUESTED)

No test file changed in this revision. No AC outcome and no lifecycle ledger entry changed; the ledger and Revision 1 above are preserved as written.

Remaining red: tests/e2e/effects-layout.spec.ts:24 ("never adds horizontal scroll while the hero elements are created at 375px"), `expect(overflow).toBeLessThanOrEqual(0)` at :38, 2 px overflow at hero t=1600. Fixes 1 and 2 from Revision 1 are confirmed green (vitest 390/390, e2e 212/213).

Classification: implementation defect, not a bad test. The test asserts AC-4 (the page never scrolls horizontally; the overlay adds no document width) with a limit of 0, which the PRD and Stage 2 require. No test change is legitimate: the only edits that would turn it green are loosening the limit or skipping it, and both are forbidden.

Defect location (confirmed by reading the CSS):
- src/styles/build-layer.css:307-310 and 317-320: `.sp-select-handle:nth-child(2)` and `:nth-child(4)` use `right: -3px`, so the right-hand 6 px corner squares stick out 3 px past the right edge of a selection box that reaches the viewport edge (about 2 px of scrollWidth at 375 px).
- src/styles/build-layer.css:276-283 (`.sp-build-fx`) and 1-9 (`.sp-build-layer`): neither clips horizontally, so the overhang extends the document's scrollable width.

Recovery belongs to the Implementer: `overflow-x: clip` on `.sp-build-layer` and `.sp-build-fx`, or inset the right-hand handles at the viewport edge. The limit stays at 0 and the test must not be loosened. Static confirmation only: the exact overflowing element was not measured in this session.

